# cloak/fur: the Fur mantle (OUTER, P2b wave 2; the warlord's, the northern traveller's): a short cloak to the waist
# under a thick fur collar (cloak/fur_front: the person's leather ramp, browns to black, in lumpy lit tufts); too short
# to fold on a seat, it keeps its rest drape there.
# It hangs behind the body (over it facing up) and rides the hang channel, so every clip's hang key moves it with the
# skirts: the hem sways by whole rows on the front and back walks (sway 3), kicks back on the side walk's contact frames
# (wide), flies in the run (flare), folds on a seat (sit) or a saddle (ride), pools on the ground (kneel, floor) and lies spread
# under a corpse (lie). 20 px across, 16 px deep at most, so the cloaked look's atlases stay near B10's budgets.
# Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body adult
role cloak fur
layer cloakBack
anchor neck
keys hang
sway 3
legend Q cloak 0
legend R cloak 1
legend S cloak 2
legend T cloak 3
legend U cloak 4

view D key rest origin 10 0
|..QTTSSSSSSSSSSRRQ..
|.QTTSSSSSSSSSSSSRRQ.
|QTTRRRRRRRRRRRRRRSRQ
|QTTRRRRRRRRRRRRRRSRQ
|QTSRRRRRRRRRRRRRRSRQ
|QTSRRRRRRRRRRRRRRSRQ
|QTTRRRRRRRRRRRRRRSRQ
|QTSRRRRRRRRRRRRRRSSQ
|QTTTTTTSSSSSSSSSSSRQ
|.QQQQQQQQQQQQQQQQQQ.
# (ARMOUR fix r1, cloakgen.py) the officer's cloak (T4, PLAN D73, STYLE_P2 29.11): `cloak.t4,!cloak.t5`
# views from the long cloak's, as wide as the T3 cape to the coat's hem facing D, inside the legs below it,
# 4 columns behind the back to the ankle facing R / L; placed before the first replacing view
view D key rest origin 14 0 when cloak.t4,!cloak.t5,!armour.t1,woman,skirt-strips replace
